!96!Blizzard Edit Mode integration
!320!On (default): MSUF Edit Mode can move the Blizzard Minimap, Chat, Micro Menu and Tooltip through the game's own Edit Mode layout. If a Blizzard preset is active, selecting an element creates and activates a saved 'MSUF' layout automatically.
!96!DandersFrames Edit Mode integration
!320!On (default): MSUF Edit Mode can move the DandersFrames party and raid containers and free pinned sets. Sets glued to the frames follow them, and DandersFrames remains the owner of all saved positions.
!96!Details! Edit Mode integration
!320!On (default): MSUF Edit Mode can move every active Details! window. Windows snapped together by Details! move as one native group.
!96!Dominos Edit Mode integration
!320!On (default): MSUF Edit Mode can move every Dominos bar that is not docked to another bar. Docked bars follow their host bar, and Dominos remains the owner of all bar positions.
!96!Grid2 Edit Mode integration
!320!On (default): MSUF Edit Mode can move the Grid2 layout and its active detached groups. Grid2 remains the owner of its layout and saved positions.
!96!Aura tooltip caster names
!320!On: aura tooltips name who applied the aura, coloured by reaction or class, through the game's own 12.1.5 option, and MSUF re-enables it after every login. Off (default): MSUF never touches the game option, so other addons or a manual console setting keep control; turning this switch off clears the option once.
!96!Aura tooltip spell IDs
!320!On: aura tooltips show the numeric spell ID through the game's own 12.1 option, and MSUF re-enables that option after every login because the game forgets it between sessions. Off (default): MSUF never touches the game option, so other addons or a manual console setting keep control; turning this switch off clears the option once.
